From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: qcom: require full-profile Uke wake IRQ providers

Uke full Type-C uses the exact OEM DP/DM and SuperSpeed PDC wake lines.
Do not silently accept missing/deferred IRQs and then suspend without them.
The separate peripheral profile retains its existing optional IRQ behavior.

Source: MiCode/kernel_devicetree 94c84aeb9e517dbde546fc732033c184094c8e57
License: GPL-2.0-only

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index 678830a..07ba14b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -478,6 +478,8 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_setup_port_irq(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom,
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	irq = platform_get_irq_byname_optional(pdev, irq_name);
+	if (qcom->uke_typec && irq <= 0)
+		return irq < 0 ? irq : -EINVAL;
 	if (irq > 0) {
 		ret = dwc3_qcom_request_irq(qcom, irq, irq_name);
 		if (ret)
@@ -493,6 +495,8 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_setup_port_irq(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom,
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	irq = platform_get_irq_byname_optional(pdev, irq_name);
+	if (qcom->uke_typec && irq <= 0)
+		return irq < 0 ? irq : -EINVAL;
 	if (irq > 0) {
 		ret = dwc3_qcom_request_irq(qcom, irq, irq_name);
 		if (ret)
@@ -508,6 +512,8 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_setup_port_irq(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom,
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	irq = platform_get_irq_byname_optional(pdev, irq_name);
+	if (qcom->uke_typec && irq <= 0)
+		return irq < 0 ? irq : -EINVAL;
 	if (irq > 0) {
 		ret = dwc3_qcom_request_irq(qcom, irq, irq_name);
 		if (ret)
